A $d$-dimensional convex polytope is centrally symmetric if, after translating its centre to the origin, $P=-P$. Faces are intersections with supporting hyperplanes, together with the polytope itself. Count all nonempty faces, of every dimension from 0 to $d$, but not the empty face. The proposed bound is $\sum_{j=0}^{d}f_j(P)\geq3^d$. \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]} \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.09215}{[S2]}

